 "ada \\2026\\11 November\\11-17-26_Daily.pdf": {
  "status": 200,
  "text": " \n \n \n \n  \nBOARD OF ADA COUNTY COMMISSIONERS \nAGENDA FOR TUESDAY, NOVEMBER 17, 2026 \n(Times Posted are Subject to Change) \n \n \nCOMMISSIONERS\u2019 CONFERENCE ROOM \n(unless otherwise noted)   \n \n \nI. CALL TO ORDER \nII. ROLL CALL \n \nACTION ITEMS: \nIII. CHANGES TO THE AGENDA  \nIV. NEW BUSINESS \n 9:00 AM \u2022 Open Business Meeting (see separate agenda) * \n             9:15 AM   \u2022     Emergency Medical Services District Open Business Meeting  \n   (see separate agenda) * \n 9:30 AM \u2022 Legal Staff/Executive Session (Idaho Code \u00a7 74-206 (1)) \n 1:30 PM \u2022 Development Services \n- Review the 11/18/26 Public Hearing Agenda \nV. ADJOURNMENT \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\uf068   \uf068   \uf068 \n \n*Denotes public meetings that may be watched live at: \nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmREyet73vxhBFCffWClEKA \n \nExecutive Sessions may be held pursuant to Idaho Code \u00a7 74-206 as needed.  The purpose of such sessions \nshall be announced at the time such sessions are called.  \n \nAny person needing special accommodation to participate in the above noticed meeting(s) should contact \nthe Ada County Commissioners\u2019 Office prior to the meeting at 287-7000. \nADA COUNTY \nCOMMISSIONERS\u2019 \nOFFICE \n200 W. Front Street \nBoise, Idaho 83702 \n(208) 287-7000 \nFax: (208) 287-7009 \nbocc1@adacounty.id.gov \nwww.adacounty.id.gov \n "
 },
 "ada \\2026\\11 November\\11-18-26_Daily.pdf": {
  "status": 200,
  "text": " \n \n \n \n  \nBOARD OF ADA COUNTY COMMISSIONERS \nAGENDA FOR WEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 18, 2026 \n(Times Posted are Subject to Change) \n \n \nCOMMISSIONERS\u2019 CONFERENCE ROOM \n(unless otherwise noted)   \n \n \n \nI. CALL TO ORDER \nII. ROLL CALL \n \nACTION ITEMS: \nIII. CHANGES TO THE AGENDA  \nIV. NEW BUSINESS \n 1:30 PM \u2022 Indigent Services (see separate agenda) \n 4:00 PM \u2022 COMPASS Legislative Forum - Meridian  \n 6:00 PM \u2022 Public Hearing - Public Hearing Room (see separate agenda) * \nV. ADJOURNMENT \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\uf068   \uf068   \uf068 \n \n*Denotes public meetings that may be watched live at: \nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmREyet73vxhBFCffWClEKA \n \nExecutive Sessions may be held pursuant to Idaho Code \u00a7 74-206 as needed.  The purpose of such sessions \nshall be announced at the time such sessions are called.  \n \nAny person needing special accommodation to participate in the above noticed meeting(s) should contact \nthe Ada County Commissioners\u2019 Office prior to the meeting at 287-7000. \n \nADA COUNTY \nCOMMISSIONERS\u2019 \nOFFICE \n200 W. Front Street \nBoise, Idaho 83702 \n(208) 287-7000 \nFax: (208) 287-7009 \nbocc1@adacounty.id.gov \nwww.adacounty.id.gov \n "
 },
 "ada \\2026\\11 November\\11-18-26_Public_Hearing_with_Staff_Links.pdf": {
  "status": 200,
  "text": "1 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nBOARD OF ADA COUNTY COMMISSIONERS \nPUBLIC HEARING AGENDA \nWEDNESDAY, NOVEMBER 18, 2026 \n6:00 P.M. \n(*Time Posted is Subject to Change) \n \n1ST FLOOR PUBLIC HEARING ROOM \n \n \n \nI. CALL TO ORDER \n \nII. ROLL CALL  \n \nACTION ITEMS: \n \nIII. CHANGES TO THE AGENDA \n \nIV. NEW BUSINESS \n1. 202300532-MSP-TE, KM ENGINEERING: Board-level Time Extension request to \ncomplete improvements for an approved Contractor's Yard. The property is located at \n4255 S Banner St and contains 0.85 acres in the Airport Industrial (M3) District; \nSection 30, T.3N, R.2E. Amelia Haynes, Associate Pla nner, at either (208) 287- 5715 \nor ahaynes@adacounty.id.gov. \n \nStaff Recommendation: Approval \nStaff: Amelia Haynes (208) 287-5715 \n \n2. 202301250-S-TE, KM ENGINEERING : A Board Level Time Extension for a \nPreliminary Plat and Private Road for a three (3) lot subdivision. The property is located \nat 6001 W Hubbard Rd and contains 30.37 acres in the Rural Residential (RR) District; \nSection 16, T.2N, R.1W. Brent Danielson, Senior Planner, at either (208) 287-7913 or \nbdanielson@adacounty.id.gov. \n \nStaff Recommendation: Approval \nStaff: Brent Danielson (208) 287-7913 \n \nADA COUNTY \nCOMMISSIONERS\u2019 \nOFFICE \n200 W. Front Street \nBoise, Idaho 83702 \n(208) 287-7000 \nFax: (208) 287-7009 \nbocc1@adacounty.id.gov \nwww.adacounty.id.gov \n \nFindings Report \nFindings Staff Report \n \n2 \n \n \n \n \n3. 202600934-S-PBA-AC-PR-V, RODNEY EVANS & PARTNERS, LLC : An \napplication for a two (2) lot subdivision along with a private road, accessory use \napplication for a large home occupation (bridal shop), property boundary adjustment, \nand a variance for minimum lot size and for existing structures to encroach into the side \nyard setbacks. The property consists of approximately 17.45 acres and is located at \n5688, 5720, and 5956 W. Overland Road in Section 16, T. 3N, R. 1W. Brent Danielson, \nSenior Planner, at either (208) 287-7913 or bdanielson@adacounty.id.gov.  \n \nP&Z Recommendation: Approval  \nStaff: Brent Danielson (208) 287-7913 \n \n \n4. 202600819-ZC-DA-S-PR, ACKERMAN-ESTVOLD: An application for approval of \na zoning ordinance map amendment, a development agreement, a preliminary plat for \nthe Voluntarist Ridge Subdivision, and a private road to rezone the property from the \nRural Urban Transition (RUT) District to the Estate Resid ential (R1) District and \nsubdivide the property into three (3) lots with the expansion of an existing private road \n(S. Wots Lane). The property is 4.993 acres within the Lineage Estates Subdivision at \n7800 S. Wots Lane, Meridian, ID 83642; Section 4, T.2N., R.1E. Kristy Inselman, \nPlanning Manager \u2013 208-287-7950 or kinselman@adacounty.id.gov. \n \nStaff Recommendation: Denial \nP&Z Recommendation: Approval  \nStaff: Kristy Inselman (208) 287-7950 \n \n \nV. RECESS \n \n \n \n\uf068   \uf068   \uf068 \n \nPublic Hearing may be watched live on the Ada County YouTube Channel: \nhttps://www.youtube.com/channel/UCmREyet73vxhBFCffWClEKA \n \nExecutive Sessions may be held pursuant to Idaho Code \u00a7 74-206 as needed during regularly scheduled \nmeetings.  The purpose of such sessions shall be announced at the time such sessions are called. \n \nAny person needing special accommodation to participate in the above noticed meeting should contact \nthe Ada County Commissioners\u2019 Office prior to the meeting at 287-7000. \nFindings Report \nFindings Report "
 },
 "ada \\2026\\2026 ANNUAL REGULAR MEETING NOTICE.pdf": {
  "status": 200,
  "text": " \n \nNOTICE OF THE 2026 REGULAR MEETING SCHEDULE FOR THE  \nBOARD OF THE ADA COUNTY COMMISSIONERS \n \n \nPursuant to Idaho Code \u00a7 74-204(1), notice is hereby given to the public that regular meetings of \nthe Board of the Ada County Commissioners for the 2026 calendar year shall be held: \n \nMondays at 8:00 a.m. or a s soon thereafter as the Board may convene, in the Commissioners\u2019 \nConference Room 3255, located in the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 \nW. Front Street., Boise, Idaho 83702, unless otherwise posted, and continue until the business then \nbefore the Board has been completed; \n \nTuesdays at 8:00 a.m. or a s soon thereafter as the Board may convene, in the Commissioners\u2019 \nConference Room 3255, located in the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 \nW. Front Street., Boise, Idaho 83702, unless otherwise posted, and continue until the business then \nbefore the Board has been completed; \n \nWednesdays at 8:00 a.m. or as soon thereafter as the Board may convene, in the Commissioners\u2019 \nConference Room 3255, located in the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 \nW. Front Street., Boise, Idaho 83702, unless otherwise posted, and then at 6:00 p.m. or as soon \nthereafter as the Board may convene, in the County Public Hearing Room, located on the 1st Floor \nof the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 W. Front Street., Boise, Idaho \n83702, unless otherwise posted, and cont inue until the business then before the Board has been \ncompleted but if business before the Board cannot be completed at a decent hour, the Board may \ncontinue such business before it to a date and time certain; \n \nThursdays at 8:00 a.m. or a s soon thereafter as the Board may convene, in the Commissioners\u2019 \nConference Room 3255, located in the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 \nW. Front Street., Boise, Idaho 83702, unless otherwise posted, and continue until the business then \nbefore the Board has been completed; \n \nFridays at 8:00 a.m. or a s soon thereafter as the Board may convene, in the Commissioners\u2019 \nConference Room 3255, located in the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 \nW. Front Street., Boise, Idaho 83702, unless otherwise posted, and continue until the business then \nbefore the Board has been completed. \n \nThe Board\u2019s regular meetings may include executive session(s), if necessary, and such other \nbusiness as shall lawfully come before the Board. \n \nDaily and meeting agendas will be posted outside the Commissioners\u2019 office and our website: \nhttps://apps.adacounty.id.gov/adafilebrowse/default.aspx?name=boccagendas by 5:00 p.m. each \nFriday or a minimum of 48 hours prior to the meeting date, as appropriate. \n \n \nNOTICE OF THE 2026 REGULAR MEETING SCHEDULE FOR THE  \nBOARD OF THE ADA COUNTY EMERGENCY MEDICAL SERVICES DISTRICT \n \nPursuant to Idaho Code \u00a7 74-204(1), notice is hereby given to the public that regular meetings of \nthe Board of the Ada County Emergency Medical Services District for the 2026 calendar year shall \nbe held every Tuesday at 9:15 a.m. in the Commissioners\u2019 Conference Room, Room 3255, located \nin the Ada County Courthouse and Administration Building, 200 W. Front Street, Boise, Idaho \n83702, unless otherwise posted, and continue until the business then before the Board has been \ncompleted.   \n \nThe Board\u2019s regular meetings may include executive sessions(s), if necessary, and such other \nbusiness as shall lawfully come before the Board."
 },
